ng  um some some sort of rather harder edged  british movies that were coming out in  the late 60s  and you know darling and um  you know uh dirk bogart's movies there  was something really  you know the servant all those films  but that was to do with a style that  completely caught my imagination and and  i remember being very aware that dirk  bogart  for instance always struck me as being  the quintessential film actor  um i never saw him perform on stage and  i don't think he performed on stage at  all very often  but on film he was he seemed like  quintessentially  um what film acting how what it could be  you know and and as as i got older i  thought that the list of people who were  inspiring me got bigger and bigger but  those are the two moments i think when i  was really aware of something  something happening that was kind of  specific
 

